1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,319
MCP before July 28, 2026:

2
00:00:03,319 --> 00:00:05,674
your server quit, you lost your order;

3
00:00:05,674 --> 00:00:09,357
now any server takes it, but how, and why, in 60 seconds?

4
00:00:09,857 --> 00:00:11,259
Here's how, in one diner.

5
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:13,410
Your AI app is the customer;

6
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:16,475
an MCP server is the waiter bringing its tools.

7
00:00:16,775 --> 00:00:18,180
Old MCP: shake hands,

8
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,733
maybe get a table number, a session ID,

9
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:22,904
and your order lives in his head.

10
00:00:23,204 --> 00:00:24,777
Other waiters: not my table.

11
00:00:25,727 --> 00:00:27,436
The new MCP drops both.

12
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:30,165
Every request is now a complete order slip,

13
00:00:30,165 --> 00:00:31,655
so any waiter can take it.

14
00:00:31,955 --> 00:00:32,976
Need a basket kept?

15
00:00:33,276 --> 00:00:35,067
The server hands back a ticket;

16
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:36,634
your AI shows it next time.

17
00:00:37,134 --> 00:00:40,261
For you, AI tools can stop hanging on one machine:

18
00:00:40,261 --> 00:00:41,671
busy day, add servers;

19
00:00:41,671 --> 00:00:44,307
one quits, the next takes your next order.

20
00:00:44,606 --> 00:00:46,687
And the ticket stays in your chat for tomorrow.

21
00:00:47,187 --> 00:00:49,419
How? The order moved onto the slip.

22
00:00:49,719 --> 00:00:51,635
Why? Any waiter can take it.

23
00:00:51,935 --> 00:00:52,925
That's stateless:

24
00:00:52,925 --> 00:00:54,686
a server that remembers nothing

25
00:00:54,686 --> 00:00:56,446
is a server anyone can replace.

26
00:00:56,946 --> 00:00:58,348
Subscribe for the next one.
